Chapter 4: Normalizing the Data
Normalization is a preprocessing technique used to bring features with different units or ranges to a comparable scale. This is essential before applying machine learning algorithms or comparative statistical analysis.
Method used: Min-Max Normalization
The formula scales each value to a [0, 1] range:
X_norm = (X - X_min) / (X_max - X_min)
Min-Max normalization was applied to all numeric columns in df_cleaned. The resulting normalized DataFrame preserves the distribution shape while ensuring all features are on the same scale.

